 "result": "This repo is Tessel, a Flask-like framework. There are two mechanisms.\n\n**Defaults**\n- **Jinja globals:** `create_jinja_environment()` in `src/tessel/app.py:492-501` puts `config`, `request`, `session` and `g` into `jinja_env.globals`. The `request`, `session` and `g` entries are the context-local proxies, so imported templates and macros also see them.\n- **Default injector:** `_base_template_vars()` in `src/tessel/templating.py:21` is registered as the first injector in `Scaffold.__init__` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:184`, `{None: [_base_template_vars]}`). It swaps the `g` and `request` proxies for the real objects, for speed. It leaves `session` as the proxy so access is still tracked.\n- **When it runs:** `render_template()` and `render_template_string()` (`templating.py:125` and `:167`) call `App.fill_template_scope()` (`src/tessel/app.py:588`). That runs every injector for the app (the `None` key) and for the request's bundles, then re-applies the values passed to `render_template` so they take precedence.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n- **Decorator:** `@app.ctx_injector` is defined as `Scaffold.ctx_injector` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`. The decorated function takes no arguments and returns a dict, and its keys become template variables. On the app it applies to every template. On a bundle it applies only to that bundle's views.\n- **Bundle-wide:** `Bundle.app_ctx_injector` in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:645` registers an injector that applies to every template in the app.\n- **Plain constants or functions:** `jinja_env.globals`, which `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:825` also uses to register template globals.",
